(begin-tx "SWP-G3 — state guards that take their expected answer as an argument")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== SWP-G3 — state guards that take their expected answer as an argument · 01 · namespace ==== =
(print "--- [SWP-G3 — state guards that take their expected answer as an argument · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [SWP-G3 · 01 · asymetric / frozen-LP / sleeping-LP] ---")
;;P3.3. Three guards of the shape (enforce (= <live value> <state argument>) ...). Each takes the
;;EXPECTED answer as a parameter, so one pool gives both cells: the live value must be accepted
;;and its negation refused. A single cell would pass against a guard that ignores its argument
;;entirely, which is what this parameter shape invites.
;;
;;UEV_AsymetricState reads a GLOBAL flag and takes no pool; the other two are per-pair.
;;
;;#FIX 2026-09-10: UEV_FrozenLP and UEV_SleepingLP built their message with
;;    (format "... set to <> for this operation" [swpair state])
;;-- TWO arguments but only ONE {} placeholder, and a literal <> where the second belonged. Pact
;;silently drops the extra argument, so the caller was told the flag must be "<>". Verified by
;;rendering it before changing anything. The placeholder is corrected, and these assertions pin
;;the corrected text.
;;==== SWP-G3 — state guards that take their expected answer as an argument · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [SWP-G3 — state guards that take their expected answer as an argument · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (let
        (
            (asym:bool (ref-SWP::UR_Asymetric))
            (frz:bool (ref-SWP::UR_IzFrozenLP pool))
            (slp:bool (ref-SWP::UR_IzSleepingLP pool))
        )
        (map print
            [
                ;;--- accepting cells: each guard agrees with the live value
                (expect "<<SWP-G3>> all three guards accept the LIVE state"
                    true (!= "" (format "{}{}{}"
                        [(ref-SWP::UEV_AsymetricState asym)
                         (ref-SWP::UEV_FrozenLP pool frz)
                         (ref-SWP::UEV_SleepingLP pool slp)])))
                ;;--- rejecting cells: each on the negation of its own flag
                (expect-failure "<<SWP-G3>> UEV_AsymetricState rejects the state the pool is NOT in"
                    "Asymetric Liquidity must be set to" (ref-SWP::UEV_AsymetricState (not asym)))
                (expect-failure "<<SWP-G3>> UEV_FrozenLP rejects the state the pool is NOT in"
                    "must have its Frozen-LP set to" (ref-SWP::UEV_FrozenLP pool (not frz)))
                (expect-failure "<<SWP-G3>> UEV_SleepingLP rejects the state the pool is NOT in"
                    "must have its Sleeping-LP set to" (ref-SWP::UEV_SleepingLP pool (not slp)))
            ]
        )
        ""
    )
)
(commit-tx)

