(begin-tx "SWP-G9 — SWPU smart-swap admission: four ways a route is refused before any token moves")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [SWP-G9 · 01 · smart-swap route admission] ---")
;;SWPU|X>SMART-SWAP is the entry to multi-hop routing, and its four opening guards are the only
;;thing standing between a caller and a swap executed along a route that does not exist.
;;
;;TECHNIQUE. These are defcaps; `test-capability` acquires one directly and runs its body, so the
;;full Talos swap flow is not needed. The four guards run in order, each masking the ones after
;;it, so every case below is built to SATISFY its predecessors and fail exactly one:
;;
;;   1  (!= input-id output-id)                    same token both sides
;;   2  (contains input-id  all-pool-tokens)       a token in no pool at all
;;   3  (contains output-id all-pool-tokens)       ...on the output side
;;   4  (!= (length edges) 0)                      two real tokens, but an empty route
;;
;;Case 4 is the interesting one: BOTH tokens are real and on pools, so the first three pass and
;;the only thing wrong is that the hopper carries no edges. Testing with a ghost token would have
;;landed on guard 2 and left guard 4 untouched.
;;
;;ONE TRANSACTION IS SAFE HERE, unlike the DALOS gas-station block: a granted capability is cached
;;per (capability, ARGUMENTS), and every call below differs in its arguments, so each re-runs the
;;body. Identical arguments would return the cached grant and silently pass.
;;==== SWP-G9 — SWPU smart-swap admission: four ways a route is refused before any token moves · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [SWP-G9 — SWPU smart-swap admission: four ways a route is refused before any token moves · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<SWP-G9>> a swap from a token to ITSELF is refused"
            "Input and Output tokens must differ"
            (test-capability (SWPU.SWPU|X>SMART-SWAP "a" "OURO-98c486052a51" 1.0
                "OURO-98c486052a51" (SWPI.UDC_Hopper [] [] []))))
        (expect-failure "<<SWP-G9>> an INPUT token that sits in no pool is refused"
            "does not exist in any Swap Pool"
            (test-capability (SWPU.SWPU|X>SMART-SWAP "a" "GHOST-000000000000" 1.0
                "OURO-98c486052a51" (SWPI.UDC_Hopper [] [] []))))
        (expect-failure "<<SWP-G9>> ...and likewise on the OUTPUT side"
            "does not exist in any Swap Pool"
            (test-capability (SWPU.SWPU|X>SMART-SWAP "a" "OURO-98c486052a51" 1.0
                "GHOST-000000000000" (SWPI.UDC_Hopper [] [] []))))
        ;;both tokens real, both on pools -- so guards 1-3 pass and only the empty route is wrong
        (expect-failure "<<SWP-G9>> two REAL tokens with an empty route trip the PATH guard, not the membership ones"
            "No path found between"
            (test-capability (SWPU.SWPU|X>SMART-SWAP "a" "OURO-98c486052a51" 1.0
                "DLK-98c486052a51" (SWPI.UDC_Hopper [] [] []))))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

