(begin-tx "SWP-G10 — SWPU|X>SWAP: single-pool admission, membership on both sides of the trade")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [SWP-G10 · 01 · single-pool swap admission] ---")
;;The single-pool entry checks the OUTPUT token's membership up front and each INPUT token's
;;membership inside the per-index map. Those are two distinct guards with two distinct messages,
;;and it would be easy to assume one covers the other -- so both are driven, each with the other
;;side held valid.
;;==== SWP-G10 — SWPU|X>SWAP: single-pool admission, membership on both sides of the trade · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [SWP-G10 — SWPU|X>SWAP: single-pool admission, membership on both sides of the trade · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
;;==== SWP-G10 — SWPU|X>SWAP: single-pool admission, membership on both sides of the trade · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [SWP-G10 — SWPU|X>SWAP: single-pool admission, membership on both sides of the trade · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect-failure "<<SWP-G10>> an OUTPUT token not on the pool is refused"
                "is not part of SwapPool"
                (test-capability (SWPU.SWPU|X>SWAP pool
                    (U|SWP.UDC_DirectSwapInputData ["DLK-98c486052a51"] [1.0] "GHOST-000000000000"))))
            (expect-failure "<<SWP-G10>> ...and an INPUT token not on the pool trips the per-index guard"
                "is not part of Liquidity Pool"
                (test-capability (SWPU.SWPU|X>SWAP pool
                    (U|SWP.UDC_DirectSwapInputData ["GHOST-000000000000"] [1.0] "OURO-98c486052a51"))))
            ;;arity: one input id against two amounts. Both ids are valid pool members, so this is
            ;;attributable to the length check and not to membership.
            (expect-failure "<<SWP-G10>> one input id against two amounts is refused"
                "Invalid input Values"
                (test-capability (SWPU.SWPU|X>SWAP pool
                    (U|SWP.UDC_DirectSwapInputData ["DLK-98c486052a51"] [1.0 2.0] "OURO-98c486052a51"))))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
;;NOT PINNED, recorded rather than left silent: "Pool {} swap functionality is inactive" and its
;;smart-swap twin "Pool {} along the Smart Swap path has swap functionality inactive" both need a
;;pool with can-swap FALSE. Every pool in this suite has swapping enabled, and SPWU|C>TOGGLE-SWAP
;;-- the cap that would turn one off -- is itself unpinned for the same reason. One toggle-off in
;;a dedicated transaction would close all three at once.
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "SWP-G11a — turn a pool's swap capability OFF (the fixture the inactive guards need)")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [SWP-G11a · 01 · disable swapping on the standard pool] ---")
;;Two guards -- one in SWPU|X>SWAP, one in the smart-swap path loop -- fire only when a pool's
;;can-swap flag is FALSE, and every pool in this suite ships with swapping enabled. This is the
;;reversible-flag shape: turn it off, assert both refusals, turn it back on and assert the pool
;;is usable again. Nothing downstream inherits a disabled pool.
;;
;;Turning swapping OFF is unguarded by design -- SPWU|C>TOGGLE-SWAP only enforces a worth floor
;;when turning it ON, because a pool that has drained below the floor must be stoppable but must
;;not be restartable. That asymmetry is what makes this fixture cheap in one direction.
;;
;;NOTE: the toggle is called WITHOUT a (try …) wrapper. It writes to SWP|Pairs, and Pact forbids
;;database writes inside `try` -- the attempt fails with "Operation disallowed in read-only or
;;sys-only mode", and that error is itself uncatchable.
;;==== SWP-G11a — turn a pool's swap capability OFF (the fixture the inactive guards need) · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [SWP-G11a — turn a pool's swap capability OFF (the fixture the inactive guards need) · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
;;==== SWP-G11a — turn a pool's swap capability OFF (the fixture the inactive guards need) · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [SWP-G11a — turn a pool's swap capability OFF (the fixture the inactive guards need) · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-C3:module{TalosStageOne_ClientThreeV4} TS01-C3)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<SWP-G11a>> swapping starts ENABLED on this pool" true (ref-SWP::UR_CanSwap pool))
        ]
    )
    (ref-TS01-C3::SWP|C_ToggleSwapCapability KST.ANHD pool false)
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<SWP-G11a>> ...and is now disabled" false (ref-SWP::UR_CanSwap pool))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
