                         (- stoa-before (coin.get-balance stoa-acct))])
                    (expect "<<SWP-I9>> the STOA quote equals the STOA charged, two modules down"
                        (- stoa-before (coin.get-balance stoa-acct))
                        (at "stoa-need" (at "stoa" predicted)))
                    (expect "<<SWP-I9>> ...and enabling the lane is NOT free in STOA"
                        true (> (- stoa-before (coin.get-balance stoa-acct)) 0.0))
                    ;;WAS A FINDING — the IGNIS halves did NOT agree, same root cause as
                    ;;`modules/VST.repl <<VST-I1>>`: both of these previews route through
                    ;;`VST::URCi_CreateSpecial*FungibleLink`, and it USED to over-quote by ~119: the
                    ;;reader added a `vst-link` deterrence the exec never charged, while under-modelling
                    ;;the transfer-role toggle as a hand-made 4.0 against a real 59.0. Wrong in opposite
                    ;;directions, so it was pinned as a FINDING rather than guessed at.
                    ;;
                    ;;RESOLVED 2026-09-14 by the owner's design call: a special link costs a small
                    ;;DETERRENCE plus payment IN FULL for the token it issues. The exec was
                    ;;under-collecting the deterrence (a revenue bug) and the preview was under-modelling
                    ;;the toggle; both are corrected in `11_VST.pact`, with the deterrence now read from
                    ;;ONE source both sides call. Full write-up at `modules/VST.repl <<VST-I1>>`.
                    ;;This block is one of the SEVEN previews that share the reader pair, so it is the
                    ;;independent check that the repair holds through SWP's own call path and not just
                    ;;through VST's.
                    (expect "<<SWP-I9>> the IGNIS quote equals the IGNIS charged"
                        (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
                        (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis" predicted)))
                ]
            )
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

