(begin-tx "SWP-I14 — INFO_SWP|AddLiquidity: the quote is exact, and 200 IGNIS still leaves the account")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [SWP-I14 · 01 · add liquidity: separating the gas quote from the asymmetry tax] ---")
;;FUNCTION COVERAGE (G6) — `INFO_SWP|AddLiquidity`, per the owner's spec: an INFO_ must report the
;;same cost the op actually charges. Template: `modules/ATS.repl <<ATS-I1>>`; the patron/interactor
;;hazard that decides whether such a measurement is valid at all is written out at <<SWP-I2>>.
;;
;;ARITY DIVERGENCE — the preview takes a FIFTH argument, `stoa-pid`, that the exec does not:
;;`SWP|C_AddLiquidity` derives it internally from `U|CT::UR_STOA-PID|Price` (`04_TS01-C3.pact:655`).
;;Feeding the preview that same reader is the only way the two are comparable; a literal there would
;;be measuring the preview against a different oracle reading than the exec used.
;;
;;WHAT THE NAIVE FORM OF THIS TEST REPORTS, AND WHY IT IS WRONG.
;;A plain balance-delta says quoted 1118.83, charged 1318.83 — a 200 IGNIS under-quote, which looks
;;exactly like the missing-leg defect found four times tonight. It is not one. `URC_STOA-PID|CLAD`
;;returns `mt-ids` / `mt-amt` — the tokens the account SENDS INTO the pool — and on an asymmetric
;;addition that list carries the IGNIS token itself:
;;    mt-ids = [GAS DLK OURO DWK]      mt-amt = [200.0 10.0 10.0 10.0]
;;That 200 is the ASYMMETRY TAX (gaseous + deficit + special legs of the CLAD), and it leaves the
;;account as PRINCIPAL through `XI_AddLiqSendAndMint`, not as gas through `IGNIS::XE_CollectIgnis`. It lands
;;in the same balance the meter reads, so it counterfeits a preview defect.
;;
;;This is the hazard already written down for `AQP-FVT|Inject` ("never measure GAS on an op whose
;;reward token is GAS") reappearing where nobody declared a reward token at all — here the protocol
;;chose IGNIS as the tax currency, and the meter cannot tell tax from fee.
;;
;;SO THE ASSERTION IS SPLIT, and both halves are worth having:
;;  1. real MINUS the declared IGNIS leg of `mt-amt` == the quote, exactly. The gas preview is right.
;;  2. that IGNIS leg is NON-ZERO here, so half 1 is not a disguised no-op.
;;
;;  3. and the third half, FIXED 2026-09-14: the preview now DECLARES the 200.
;;
;;THE DEFECT THAT WAS: nothing in `ClientInfo` surfaced that 200. A client who funded exactly
;;`ignis-need` and called the op ran out of IGNIS, because the tax was invisible to the preview
;;surface. `URCi_AddStandardLiquidity`'s @doc says "the CLAD PERFECT-ignis-fee", so the omission was
;;deliberate and documented; the client-facing consequence was not.
;;
;;THE FIX, and why it went into `pre-text` rather than into `ignis-need`. `ignis-need` is what the
;;IGNIS collector will take as GAS, and the whole billing chain — discount, quarter-split, the
;;OutputCumulator itself — is built around that meaning. Folding a principal transfer into it would
;;make the number wrong for the thing it is actually used for, and would silently re-discount a tax
;;that is not discounted. So the tax is DECLARED instead, in the same `pre-text` the launchpad
;;previews use to declare amounts, and it is declared from the SAME CLAD the charge is computed from
;;(`SWPLC::URCi_Add*LiquidityClad`, new single-source readers) so a client reads one number and the
;;pool takes that number.
;;
;;WHAT PINS IT: the assertion below does not compare the declaration to another reader. It formats
;;the MEASURED tax — the figure that satisfies `predicted + tax = real` two lines up, i.e. the IGNIS
;;that provably left the account — and requires the preview's own prose to contain it. If the
;;declaration ever drifts from the charge (say the two CLAD collection flags diverge), the substring
;;stops matching.
;;
;;The gaseous leg is deliberately NOT part of the declared tax: it is billed through the cumulator
;;as gas, so it is already inside `ignis-need`. Its wording is carried in `pre-text` for completeness
;;and the log line below shows the full surface.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-C3:module{TalosStageOne_ClientThreeV4} TS01-C3)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (ref-SWPL:module{SwapperLiquidityV2} SWPL)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-U|LST:module{StringProcessorV2} U|LST)
        (ref-U|CT|DIA:module{DiaStoaPidV2} U|CT)
        (sd:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
        (amounts:[decimal] [10.0 10.0 10.0])
    )
    (let
        (
            (ignis-id:string (ref-DALOS::UR_IgnisID))
            (clad-op:object{SwapperLiquidityV2.CladOperation}
                (at "clad-op" (ref-SWPL::URC_STOA-PID|CLAD patron sd
                    (ref-SWPL::URC_LD sd amounts) true true (ref-U|CT|DIA::UR_STOA-PID|Price))))
        )
        (let
            (
                ;;the IGNIS leg of what the account is about to SEND IN — principal, not gas
                (tax:decimal
                    (fold (+) 0.0
                        (map (lambda (idx:integer)
                                (if (= (at idx (at "mt-ids" clad-op)) ignis-id)
                                    (at idx (at "mt-amt" clad-op))
                                    0.0))
                             (enumerate 0 (- (length (at "mt-ids" clad-op)) 1)))))
                (info:object{OuronetInfoV2.ClientInfo}
                    (INFO-ONE.INFO_SWP|AddLiquidity patron patron sd amounts
                        (ref-U|CT|DIA::UR_STOA-PID|Price)))
                (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
            )
            (let
                (
                    (m (ref-TS01-C3::SWP|C_AddLiquidity patron patron sd amounts))
                )
                (let
                    (
                        (real:decimal (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false)))
                        (predicted:decimal (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis" info)))
                    )
                    (map print
                        [
                            (format "<<SWP-I14>> quoted={} total-ignis-out={} asymmetry-tax={} gas-only={}"
                                [predicted real tax (- real tax)])
                            (format "<<SWP-I14>> PRE-TEXT >>> {}" [(at "pre-text" info)])
                            (expect "<<SWP-I14>> INFO_SWP|AddLiquidity's quote equals the GAS the op charged"
                                (- real tax) predicted)
                            (expect "<<SWP-I14>> ...and the gas is a real, non-zero charge"
                                true (> (- real tax) 0.0))
                            ;;without this the split above would pass just as well on a symmetric add
                            (expect "<<SWP-I14>> the op ALSO takes IGNIS as an asymmetry tax, non-zero on this add"
                                true (> tax 0.0))
                            (expect "<<SWP-I14>> ...and that tax travels as mt-amt PRINCIPAL, so it is invisible to ignis-need"
                                0.0 (- (+ predicted tax) real))
                            ;;the fix: the number that provably left the account must appear, verbatim,
                            ;;in the preview's own declaration. Built from `tax`, which the line above
                            ;;ties to the measured balance delta -- so this is prose checked against a
                            ;;measurement, not against a second reader.
                            (expect "<<SWP-I14>> ...and the preview DECLARES that exact tax in its pre-text"
                                true
                                (contains (format "{} IGNIS of Asymmetric-Liquidity TAX" [tax])
                                          (concat (at "pre-text" info))))
                            (expect "<<SWP-I14>> ...and it declares the relinquished LP as principal too"
                                true
                                (contains "LP relinquished to the pool" (concat (at "pre-text" info))))
                            ;;non-vacuity for the two above: pre-text must not be the one-line
                            ;;operation description it was before the fix
                            (expect "<<SWP-I14>> ...and the declaration is additional to the operation line"
                                true (> (length (at "pre-text" info)) 1))
                        ]
                    )
                )
            )
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

