(begin-tx "SWP-I24 — INFO_SWP|AddGlacialLiquidity quote vs measured charge")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [SWP-I24 · 01 · add liquidity with a glacial secondary LP] ---")
;;FUNCTION COVERAGE (G6) — `INFO_SWP|AddGlacialLiquidity`, per the owner's spec. Template: `modules/ATS.repl <<ATS-I1>>`;
;;the patron/interactor hazard is written out at <<SWP-I2>>.
;;The glacial variant carries a ZERO-GUARD the iced one does not: when `native-lp` comes out at 0.0
;;the transfer leg collapses to EOC. Same pool as <<SWP-I23>>, so any difference is the variant itself.;;
;;NO ASYMMETRY-TAX SPLIT HERE, and the reason is worth recording. `<<SWP-I14>>` had to subtract an
;;IGNIS leg that the STANDARD add takes as principal. This variant does not take one, because the
;;CLAD collection FLAGS differ per variant: standard passes `(asymmetric-collection=true,
;;gaseous-collection=true)`, iced and glacial pass `(false, true)`. With asymmetric collection off
;;there is no IGNIS in `mt-ids` at all, so a plain balance-delta is exact — and a split copied over
;;from <<SWP-I14>> would subtract a tax that was never charged, turning a correct preview into a
;;reported defect.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-C3:module{TalosStageOne_ClientThreeV4} TS01-C3)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-U|CT|DIA:module{DiaStoaPidV2} U|CT)
        (pool:string "P|OURO-98c486052a51|BUSD-98c486052a51")
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
        (amounts:[decimal] [10.0 10.0])
    )
    (let
        (
            (predicted:decimal
                (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis"
                    (INFO-ONE.INFO_SWP|AddGlacialLiquidity patron patron pool amounts (ref-U|CT|DIA::UR_STOA-PID|Price)))))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
            (m (ref-TS01-C3::SWP|C_AddGlacialLiquidity patron patron pool amounts))
        )
        (map print
            [
                (format "<<SWP-I24>> predicted={} real={}"
                    [predicted (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))])
                (expect "<<SWP-I24>> INFO_SWP|AddGlacialLiquidity's quote equals what the op actually charged"
                    (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false)) predicted)
                (expect "<<SWP-I24>> ...and it is a real, non-zero charge"
                    true (> (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false)) 0.0))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "SWP-I25 — INFO_SWP|RemoveLiquidity quote vs measured charge")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [SWP-I25 · 01 · burn LP and take the tokens back] ---")
;;FUNCTION COVERAGE (G6) — `INFO_SWP|RemoveLiquidity`, per the owner's spec. Template: `modules/ATS.repl <<ATS-I1>>`;
;;the patron/interactor hazard is written out at <<SWP-I2>>.
;;THIS BLOCK FOUND A DEFECT (fixed 2026-09-14). The preview's flat leg read
;;`UC_IgnisPrice "SWP|C_RemoveLiquidity" "lp-churn"` = 1029.0 — the 1000.0 central deterrent PLUS
;;this op's own 29.0 component — while `C_RemoveLiquidity`'s `ico-flat` read the BARE deterrent
;;`UC_IgnisDeter "lp-churn"` = 1000.0. Every liquidity removal was therefore over-quoted by 29.0 raw
;;IGNIS (15.37 after this patron's 0.53 discount).
;;
;;WHY IT LOOKED RIGHT: the ADD sibling uses `UC_IgnisPrice` on BOTH sides and matches exactly
;;(<<SWP-I14>>, <<SWP-I22>>), and both call sites carry the same "central IG|DETER lp-churn"
;;comment. Reading either one alone confirms the other.
;;
;;RESOLVED TOWARD THE ADD SIDE (owner ruling: "make them consistent"). The disagreement was never
;;really preview-vs-exec — it was remove-vs-add. All five ADD ops bill `UC_IgnisPrice` on both sides,
;;`UC_IgnisPrice`'s own @doc says "every URCi_* reader should bill through this", and the 29.0
;;`SWP|C_RemoveLiquidity` row sat in the IGNIS price table billed by nothing at all. So the EXEC
;;moved up to `UC_IgnisPrice` rather than the preview moving down to the bare deter, and removal now
;;carries its component exactly as an add does. The removal fee rises 29.0 raw / 15.37 net.
;;<<SWP-I25b>> below pins the direction so a silent slide back to the bare deter is caught.
;;A FOUR-LEG preview: a flat removal fee + the account->SWP LP transfer + the LP burn + the
;;SWP->account multi-transfer back out. Nothing here moves IGNIS as principal, so the plain
;;balance-delta is valid — unlike the ADD side, which needed the split at <<SWP-I14>>.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-C3:module{TalosStageOne_ClientThreeV4} TS01-C3)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (ref-SWPL:module{SwapperLiquidityV2} SWPL)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (sd:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
    )
    (let
        (
            (predicted:object{OuronetInfoV2.ClientInfo} (INFO-ONE.INFO_SWP|RemoveLiquidity patron patron sd 1.0))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
            (m (ref-TS01-C3::SWP|C_RemoveLiquidity patron patron sd 1.0))
        )
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<SWP-I25>> INFO_SWP|RemoveLiquidity's quote equals what the op actually charged"
                    (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
                    (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis" predicted)))
                (expect "<<SWP-I25>> ...and it is a real, non-zero charge"
                    true (> (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false)) 0.0))
                ;;<<SWP-I25b>> the equality above would hold just as well if BOTH sides slid back to
                ;;the bare deterrent together. This names the component: the charge must exceed what
                ;;the deterrent alone plus the other three legs would cost, i.e. the 29.0 row is
                ;;genuinely billed. Written against the price table, not against a copied number.
                (expect "<<SWP-I25b>> the removal really bills its own 29.0 component, not the bare deterrent"
                    true (> (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
                            (* (ref-DALOS::URC_IgnisGasDiscount patron)
                               (IGNIS.UC_IgnisDeter "lp-churn"))))
                (expect "<<SWP-I25b>> ...and remove is priced off the same reader as add"
                    (IGNIS.UC_IgnisPrice "SWP|C_RemoveLiquidity" "lp-churn")
                    (+ (IGNIS.UC_IgnisDeter "lp-churn") 29.0))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

